================================================================================
## Port Graph Chat max_tokens fix (PR #223) to 0.10.0
================================================================================

Context: PR #223 (squash 2024650d) landed on 0.9.3. The same hardcoded
`max_tokens=2048` existed on 0.10.0, so Graph Chat still hit the
"I couldn't display that answer" fallback on reasoning models. This entry
ports the change to 0.10.0 by cherry-picking the squash commit.

Conflict resolution (0.10.0 already had `endpoint_kind` on `run_agent`):
- `run_agent()` keeps `endpoint_kind` and adds `max_tokens` after it.
- Test file keeps the existing `test_run_agent_forwards_domain_endpoint_kind`
  and adds the `max_tokens` tests.
- `baseline.json`: kept 0.10.0 values, bumped `run_agent` 198->201 and the
  two chat routes by +1 for the new parameter.

Changes:

1. src/shared/config/constants.py
   New `DTWIN_CHAT_MAX_TOKENS = 8192` (single source of truth).
2. src/shared/config/settings.py
   `dtwin_chat_max_tokens` setting (alias `ONTOBRICKS_DTWIN_CHAT_MAX_TOKENS`),
   default 8192, bounded `ge=1, le=8192`.
3. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py
   `run_agent()` takes `max_tokens` (default `DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS = 8192`)
   instead of the hardcoded 2048.
4. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   Blocking and streaming chat routes pass `settings.dtwin_chat_max_tokens`.
5. app.yaml.template
   Exposes `ONTOBRICKS_DTWIN_CHAT_MAX_TOKENS` for deployed apps.
6. docs/getting-started.md
   New "Graph Chat (Digital Twin Assistant)" env var table + `.env` example.
7. tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat_engine.py
   Engine default matches Settings default; configured max_tokens reaches
   `call_serving_endpoint`.
8. tests/units/settings/test_app_yaml_template.py
   Template value matches Settings default; out-of-bounds values rejected.
9. tests/units/architecture/baseline.json
   Size budget bumps for the new parameter.
10. changelogs/v0.10.0/diegoantonelli_2026-11-06.log
    changelogs/v0.10.0/diegoantonelli_2026-11-09.log
    Moved from changelogs/v0.9.3/ to the 0.10.0 release folder.

